# Code owners for loxilb-oam. Handles are taken from MAINTAINERS.md.
#
# Every pull request requires an approving review from these maintainers before it can be
# merged. This is enforced by the branch-protection rule on `main`
# ("Require review from Code Owners" + at least 1 approval).
#
# Every listed owner must have write access to the repository once it is created under the
# loxilb-io org, otherwise GitHub ignores them and warns. Confirm the roster for loxilb-oam before
# enabling required review. A team (e.g. @loxilb-io/loxilb-oam-maintainers) may be used instead of
# individual handles so membership can change without editing this file.
#
# Note on @loxilb-devel: it is an org-level shared development account with write access, not an
# individual maintainer, so it is deliberately not listed in MAINTAINERS.md. The roster there
# tracks people; this file tracks who must review. Do not "fix" the apparent mismatch by adding a
# row for it to MAINTAINERS.md.
#
# Ownership does not accumulate across patterns — for any given file, only the LAST matching line
# applies. That is why @loxilb-devel is repeated on the path rules below rather than being covered
# by the `*` rule alone.

*       @backguynn @inhogog2 @loxilb-devel

# CI/CD, release automation, and repo governance are the highest-value tamper
# targets (a malicious workflow change can exfiltrate secrets or ship a
# poisoned release). Call them out explicitly so a review is always required
# on these paths even if the glob above is ever narrowed.
/.github/        @backguynn @inhogog2 @NLX-SeokHwanKong @loxilb-devel
